WEBVTT

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:06.650
<b>GUNDAM
VICTORY
MOBILE SUIT</b>

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:31.030
Üso was able to obtain a new Gundam.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.260
But he was dumbfounded to learn...

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:38.260
...that his mother, Myra, was involved in its development.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.130
It was painful to learn the truth...

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:46.230
...that the adults in the League Militaire may have been hiding this from him.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.460
MOTHER'S GUNDAM

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.930
"Mother's Gundam".
MOTHER'S GUNDAM

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.530
MOTHER'S GUNDAM

00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:01.200
Your feelings are still too chaotic. Concentrate more.

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:04.900
Mother?

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.400
Now that you've mastered it with your right hand,

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.960
it's time for you to try it with your left.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:14.260
My left hand?

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:14.830
Go on.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:23.930
You're left-handed to begin with,

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:26.460
but it's best to be able to do it with either hand, right?

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.400
Yeah!

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.630
Üso, you're being surrounded!

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.800
I can use my right or left hand without any problem!

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.300
It's because you're chasing us!

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.600
If you weren't chasing us I wouldn't have to shoot you!

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:03.630
It's close!

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.930
Is that you, Miss Katejina?! Please, stop chasing me!

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:12.060
What's so great about Zanscare?!

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:14.700
So stubborn!

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.130
I won't let you escape to the moon!

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:30.260
What?!

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:34.700
Wings of light?

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.430
Katejina, what's so scary about him showing off?!

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:43.230
Why can't you just let me go see my mother?!

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:50.130
You're such a show-off. Are you trying to make a fool out of me?

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:56.560
You won't escape, League Militaire!

00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:02.860
Uh-oh! A trap?!

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.830
Damn! He scattered micro-mines!

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.230
Miss Marbet!

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:22.200
Looks like having everyone scatter mines worked.

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:24.500
And because Shrike Team's still going strong.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.230
The carrier did well.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:31.200
Because you've gotten better at coordinated plays , Üso.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.360
It's because my machine's gotten better.

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:34.860
I'll head back to the White Ark.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.930
You do that!

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:40.430
Üso, the Reineforce Junior took considerable damage.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.200
We're going to land nearby.

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:43.560
Roger.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.500
I'll have the White Ark find an emergency landing spot.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:06.700
Looks like Üso's mastered the new Victory.

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.930
He really is unusual, huh?

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.530
We're not going to Saint Josef?

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:15.630
No. The Reineforce Junior's in bad shape, so it's making an emergency landing.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.000
Emergency landing?

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.160
For repairs.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.600
Now that most of our repairs are complete,

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:41.430
we can take off for Earth in sequence.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.700
Are the running tests of the Motorad Fleet going well?

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:48.660
Yes, sir. Running them on Earth won't kill us.

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:54.400
I'll be directing information gathering on the League Militaire in Saint Josef.

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.500
Pippiniden, you can confirm the test results for me.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:58.400
Yes, sir!

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.430
Prepare a buggy for us.

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.300
Sir!

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:05.800
Going for a stroll around the city?

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:08.660
Information gathering is a vital job, too.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:17.930
So, this is the moon.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:23.360
Whoops... I need to stay on guard.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:27.460
Until they get us parts for the Reineforce Junior and mobile suits.

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:30.060
What's that light?

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:31.360
Light?

00:06:31.400 --> 00:06:33.300
That light's my little brother, Karel!

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:34.630
Karel?

00:06:36.360 --> 00:06:38.630
Big brother, do you read me? It's Karel.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.400
There's a Zanscare fleet nearby,

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:44.660
so we got word not to make direct contact with the factory.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.660
Even a vessel this small is no good?

00:06:46.700 --> 00:06:47.630
No good.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.430
Since there's a way in to the factory from Saint Josef,

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:52.230
they want us to enter that way.

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:53.930
Üso, did you get all that?

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:55.560
Uh, yeah! Roger!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:04.030
Man, you could have left him behind!

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.730
Flanders didn't have to come, too!

00:07:05.760 --> 00:07:09.100
For a bunch of kids to not look suspicious, you need a dog!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.130
Flanders, come out.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.300
Say, Karel, did anyone at the Xorazm factory...

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.930
...mention someone named Myra Migelle?

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:18.360
Is she with the League Militaire?

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.300
Ow...

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:28.700
That's Saint Josef!

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:31.030
It's pretty!

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:44.560
Okay inside the car! The dog's going with you?

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:45.460
Yeah!

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.300
Hey! Try to look more cheerful!

00:07:47.830 --> 00:07:50.360
You don't want them thinking we're illegal immigrants!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:52.830
I've been a little nauseous all morning, so...

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.900
I don't blame you. There's a bad cold going around.

00:07:55.930 --> 00:07:57.460
Your face is really red.

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:01.600
And you have a fever. Take care of yourself.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:02.760
Thank you!

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:04.960
C'mon, Warren, you need to rest.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:07.060
Go see a doctor as soon as you can.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.200
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

00:08:08.230 --> 00:08:09.860
See a doctor soon, okay?

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:11.100
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.660
We'll never find anyone in here.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.200
Not like we have time for that.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.000
Front!

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:37.260
What's...

00:08:37.900 --> 00:08:38.930
They're running!

00:08:41.530 --> 00:08:42.930
What are you doing?!

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:44.430
Go after them!

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.100
We won't have time to get the mobile suits from the factory!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.260
You're always getting us involved in trouble! Stop it!

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.030
Shut up and follow them!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:03.700
Hold it right there, lady spy!

00:09:06.600 --> 00:09:09.560
You were trying to check out our tests, weren't you?!

00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:18.760
You little brat!

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:23.760
Why, you!

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.700
Hang on! Get in the truck!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.130
Shahkti?

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.600
Mrs. Myra?!

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:34.130
Hurry up!

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:35.200
Are you okay?

00:09:35.230 --> 00:09:36.460
Haro! Flanders, come!

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.360
Haro!

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:42.930
Come on!

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.830
Okay! Karel, floor it!

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.160
Üso, what are you doing here?

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:51.430
Mom! Mom, is that you?

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:53.600
Üso's mom?!

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:08.230
BESPA's secret police have infiltrated Saint Josef,

00:10:08.260 --> 00:10:10.230
but we should be safe here.

00:10:11.030 --> 00:10:13.760
If those guys before were Zanscare secret police,

00:10:13.800 --> 00:10:17.060
was it because you're working for the League Militaire, ma'am?

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:18.600
Thank you.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:21.060
It'd be better if you didn't know.

00:10:22.530 --> 00:10:23.900
Shahkti, let's go.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.630
Goodbye, and take care.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:27.560
Thank you.

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:29.630
Odelo?

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:32.330
We'll go to the factory. You stay here.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:33.130
But...

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:35.630
I'm saying, take a break, just for once!

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:36.800
R-Right...

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:41.230
That's right. You've been doing a ton of work.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:42.430
Haro, come.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:43.600
Haro!

00:10:58.330 --> 00:10:59.360
Üso!

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:04.330
Mom!

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.200
I'm sorry. I'm sorry for leaving you alone.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:10.160
Üso...

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:28.800
In order to build the new Victory on the moon,

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:31.900
I had to bring the designs here myself.

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:35.360
I won't ask for your understanding, but...

00:11:36.430 --> 00:11:38.500
I could have helped you.

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:43.700
Yes. The fact you're here now shows me that.

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:48.360
Yeah. Because I've been the Victory's pilot.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:53.530
I'd heard a child was piloting it. So, that was you.

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:57.800
Piloting a mobile suit must have been hard.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:12:02.600
But, I started out by piloting a BESPA mobile suit,

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:04.830
so the Victory wasn't that hard.

00:12:05.130 --> 00:12:08.800
But having to dock in midair during a fight was scary.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:09.960
You did that?

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:10.960
Yeah.

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:17.230
Here he comes!

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:17.930
Fire!

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:18.730
Right!

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:28.200
The thing on the Camion?!

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:29.500
Do you read me, Üso?

00:12:30.230 --> 00:12:31.830
I-I can.

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:35.800
Form your fighter up with the Hanger and Boots!

00:12:36.260 --> 00:12:39.030
The Hanger just flew by! Where are the Boots?!

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:40.060
Here they come!

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.360
Set the auto-balancer to V Mode!

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.300
Roger!

00:12:47.960 --> 00:12:49.160
It's docked?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.530
The Boots are next!

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:51.700
R-Right!

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:00.760
He was docking at the same time as me?!

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.100
They got it?!

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.000
Miss Marbet!

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:11.800
I may have more firepower, but I can barely move now!

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:13.030
Üso, listen!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.700
We're sending out another set of Boots!

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.000
They'll launch south of the signal flare.

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:18.630
Üso, come here!

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.600
Okay? Prepare to launch!

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:24.560
Miss Katejina!

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:25.360
Right!

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:27.730
Boots, launch!

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:33.560
The Boots are right behind you, Üso!

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.530
Roger! Lining up for V Mode!

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:52.600
That day, after I docked the Victory for the first time,

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:56.760
I was able to fight a mobile suit hand to hand.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:00.030
Because we raised you to be able to do that.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:04.200
Thank goodness you grew up to be such a capable child.

00:14:04.300 --> 00:14:05.830
But, I was scared!

00:14:05.960 --> 00:14:08.560
I hate not knowing what to do.

00:14:08.960 --> 00:14:11.960
I know, but you bear with it,

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:14.330
and eventually you understand what to do.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:15.530
Understand what?

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:17.130
What grownups do.

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:21.460
I understand... That BESPA and Zanscare's methods...

00:14:21.500 --> 00:14:24.700
...are unacceptable and that I can't just do nothing.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:28.830
To those who ask "Why go this far?", here is my answer.

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:32.960
We are the BESPA of Zanscare!

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.200
The Yellow Jackets of the Gatie party!

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:39.800
And so, to all who would resist Zanscare,

00:14:40.300 --> 00:14:42.760
know that this is what awaits you!

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.830
Give him the guillotine! Death to the rebel!

00:14:58.560 --> 00:15:00.400
And I know that the guillotine...

00:15:00.430 --> 00:15:04.330
...was used like a spectacle in the Pre-UC era.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:09.400
But using it now that mankind lives in space is just cruel!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:13.500
And then, after that, Victory worked even better, right?

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:17.100
Why? Why would you bring up that machine?

00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:20.160
Because that machine was made to end the guillotine's use.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.560
It all seems like a coincidence.

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:26.330
Was it just coincidence that you've survived?

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:28.230
It's not just coincidence?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.600
Exactly.

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.630
You were piloting it, right?

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:33.330
Right.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:35.730
Even then, I was piloting it.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:46.160
I think the Camion's right below us, but...

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:47.830
Miss Marbet!

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:50.660
There's no way to dock in this situation!

00:15:53.300 --> 00:15:54.360
Miss Marbet!

00:15:54.400 --> 00:15:56.530
Raise the head and increase your thrust!

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:57.830
Üso!

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:09.560
Miss Marbet, I'll switch with you!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.900
Please do, Üso.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:14.630
Come on!

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.530
Okay!

00:16:17.900 --> 00:16:18.830
Okay...

00:16:19.160 --> 00:16:20.100
Here they come!

00:16:29.030 --> 00:16:33.130
Scatter! Go away! Go somewhere else!

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:44.060
Otis, send out the Hanger!

00:16:44.660 --> 00:16:47.130
Kuffu, Ness, send out the Boots!

00:16:47.330 --> 00:16:49.800
Here it comes! Launch the Boots!

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:55.960
The Boots are here!

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:02.100
It docked?!

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:16.060
I wouldn't have gotten you if you weren't attacking!

00:17:22.860 --> 00:17:24.100
The Hanger's here?!

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:31.960
Go away!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:36.560
Go away, or you're all going to die!

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:41.700
Why, you!

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:55.600
Please tell me... oshiete watashi wa

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:59.530
It's too big to simply call it a talent

00:17:59.530 --> 00:18:01.000
Please tell me... oshiete watashi wa

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.000
...the reason I am sleeping here koko ni nemuru wake wo
You and father...

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:05.230
Yes?

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:05.260
...the reason I am sleeping here koko ni nemuru wake wo

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:07.830
Did you make me study all those things...

00:18:07.860 --> 00:18:09.430
...so I'd turn out like this?

00:18:09.930 --> 00:18:13.560
Please teach me the song umareru mae kara
We never forced you to.

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:17.000
And you were never just our child.
Please teach me the song umareru mae kara

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:17.900
That I've heard since before I was born kikoteita uta wo

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.260
What do you mean?

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:19.800
That I've heard since before I was born kikoteita uta wo

00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:22.030
That night before you were born...

00:18:22.060 --> 00:18:25.560
How do I put it? A huge white something appeared to me.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:27.300
This light that burns in my heart kokoro ni tomoru hikari wa

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:29.530
I had a dream that seemed to say that...

00:18:29.530 --> 00:18:29.560
This light that burns in my heart kokoro ni tomoru hikari wa

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:31.730
...my new child would be a Newtype.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:32.660
A Newtype?

00:18:32.700 --> 00:18:33.630
What does it illuminate? nani wo terashiteiru

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:38.860
Even a realist like your father believed in it.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:40.260
That's just...

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:41.400
Its warmth... sono nukumori wa

00:18:41.400 --> 00:18:43.860
I also believe in that dream.

00:18:43.900 --> 00:18:47.160
...travels across time and awakens toki wo koemezameru
Because you've survived to this day.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:50.730
I guess, but... Is that the reason?

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:53.730
Miss Marbet!

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:08.760
What am I doing? What am I trying to accomplish?

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:09.830
Üso!

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.800
Miss Marbet!

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:27.900
What do you think you're doing?! I thought you hated being scared!

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.600
I do, but this is just so scary.

00:19:50.660 --> 00:19:54.230
Because I'm not afraid! I won't be afraid of you!

00:19:57.930 --> 00:19:59.900
I won't be scared of your numbers!

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:20.960
Fall over!

00:20:25.330 --> 00:20:27.300
You're scared now, right? Right?!

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:29.230
Because fighting is scary!

00:20:39.930 --> 00:20:40.760
Him?

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:50.960
Not bad, white suit, but this is the end!

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:09.560
Why, you!

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:28.800
Please tell me... oshiete watashi wa

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:34.700
...the reason I am sleeping here koko ni nemuru wake wo

00:21:36.900 --> 00:21:39.600
It must have been so hard for you.
Please teach me the song umareru mae kara

00:21:39.600 --> 00:21:39.630
Please teach me the song umareru mae kara

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:44.000
But I believe that we humans have...

00:21:44.030 --> 00:21:49.430
That I've heard since before I was born kikoteita uta wo
...great abilities.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:51.900
We've suffered, too.

00:21:51.960 --> 00:21:53.160
This light that burns in my heart kokoro ni akaru hikari wa

00:21:53.160 --> 00:21:56.830
But, for raising you this way,

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:58.930
for testing you like this...

00:21:59.800 --> 00:22:00.660
What does it illuminate? nani wo terashiteiru

00:22:00.660 --> 00:22:01.960
I'm sorry.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:06.260
What does it illuminate? nani wo terashiteiru

00:22:07.100 --> 00:22:10.660
Its warmth... sono nukumori wa

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:16.630
...travels across time and awakens toki wo koemezameru

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:35.000
To prevent the Motorad Fleet from heading to Earth,

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:37.960
I decide to meet with Commandant Cronicle.

00:23:38.800 --> 00:23:42.000
Seeing BESPA's secret police take me,

00:23:42.030 --> 00:23:44.430
Üso tries to get me back,

00:23:44.700 --> 00:23:46.930
but his mother ends up getting captured...

00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:50.460
...by Miss Katejina's mobile suit in my place.

